{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#withIsExclusive\"><span class=\"name\">withIsExclusive</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> v}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Checks whether `a` is exclusive at runtime, applying `k` to the verdict. This can be used, for\nexample, to skip caching values that are not referenced from anywhere else. This function is\nsafe because of the proof obligation `h`, which ensures that the result does not depend on the\nanswer.\n \nThis function is a safe wrapper around `isExclusive`. Logically, it is `k false`. \n\nBeing exclusive does not imply that `a` can be updated in place: that also requires the caller\nto own `a` rather than borrow it.","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#withIsExclusive","kind":"def","line":187,"name":"withIsExclusive","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Util.lean#L187-L200"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">unsafe def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#withIsExclusiveUnsafe\"><span class=\"name\">withIsExclusiveUnsafe</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> v}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#withIsExclusiveUnsafe","kind":"def","line":183,"name":"withIsExclusiveUnsafe","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Util.lean#L183-L185"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#withPtrAddr\"><span class=\"name\">withPtrAddr</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> v}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">u₁ </span><span class=\"fn\">u₂</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">u₁</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">u₂</span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#withPtrAddr","kind":"def","line":179,"name":"withPtrAddr","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Util.lean#L179-L180"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#withPtrEqDecEq\"><span class=\"name\">withPtrEqDecEq</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">withPtrEq</span> : <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>) → <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span>) → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">(</a><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">)</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a>)</span> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hw</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>) (<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span>) (<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">(</a><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">)</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a></span>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">withPtrEq</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> <span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">h</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">(</a><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">)</a></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Decidable\">Decidable</a> (<span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span>)</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Decidable\">Decidable</a> (<span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span>)</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Build a `DecidableEq` instance that short-circuits using a pointer equality check where possible.\n\nUsually, `withPtrEq` is passed as the first argument, as in\n`withPtrEqDecEq withPtrEq (fun _ _ _ _ => rfl) a b k`. Since `withPtrEqDecEq` is polymorphic, it\ncannot use `withPtrEq` directly; see the docstring of `withPtrEq`.","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#withPtrEqDecEq","kind":"def","line":165,"name":"withPtrEqDecEq","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Util.lean#L165-L177"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">noncomputable def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#withPtrEq\"><span class=\"name\">withPtrEq</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">_h</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">(</a><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">)</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns `k ()`, but skips evaluating `k ()` and returns `true` if `a` and `b` are represented by the\nsame pointer at runtime.\n\nIf `k` is a function that performs an equality check on `a` and `b`, then this operation can be\nused to short-circuit the equality check for pointer-equal input.\n\nThis is only correct if pointer-equal values of `α` are equal. This is not the case if values of `α`\ncan contain types or type formers, because these are erased at runtime. For example, `True` and\n`False` have the same runtime representation, but `withPtrEq True False (fun _ => false) _` must\nreturn `false`. Therefore, the compiler refuses to compile a definition that uses `withPtrEq` unless\nit can check that values of `α` cannot contain types or type formers. In particular, `withPtrEq`\ncannot be used polymorphically: it can be used at types such as `List Nat` or `Fin n`, but not at\n`List β` if `β` is a type variable.\n\nUse `withPtrEqUnsafe` to bypass this check.","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#withPtrEq","kind":"def","line":143,"name":"withPtrEq","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Util.lean#L143-L163"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">unsafe def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#withPtrEqUnsafe\"><span class=\"name\">withPtrEqUnsafe</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">_h</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">(</a><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit.unit\">)</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns `true` if `a` and `b` are represented by the same pointer at runtime, or `k ()` otherwise.\n\nIf `k` is a function that performs an equality check on `a` and `b`, then this operation can be\nused to short-circuit the equality check for pointer-equal input.\n\nThis function is unsafe because its result is not equal to `k ()` if `α` includes computationally\nirrelevant data like types. Consider the example `α := Prop`, `a := True`, `b := False`,\n`k := fun _ => false`. In this case, `a = b → k () = true` is true, but `a` and `b` have the same\nruntime representation of an erased type, so `ptrEq a b` is true and this function returns `true`,\neven though `k ()` is `false`.\n\n`withPtrEq` is a safe version of this function, for which the compiler checks that `α` does not\ninclude such data.","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#withPtrEqUnsafe","kind":"def","line":125,"name":"withPtrEqUnsafe","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Util.lean#L125-L141"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">unsafe def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#ptrEqList\"><span class=\"name\">ptrEqList</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">as </span><span class=\"fn\">bs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Compares two lists of objects for element-wise pointer equality. Returns `true` if both lists are\nthe same length and the objects at the corresponding indices of each list are pointer-equal.\n\nTwo objects are pointer-equal if, at runtime, they are allocated at exactly the same address. This\nfunction is unsafe because it can distinguish between definitionally equal values.","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#ptrEqList","kind":"def","line":113,"name":"ptrEqList","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Util.lean#L113-L123"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">unsafe def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#ptrEq\"><span class=\"name\">ptrEq</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Compares two objects for pointer equality.\n\nTwo objects are pointer-equal if, at runtime, they are allocated at exactly the same address. This\nfunction is unsafe because it can distinguish between definitionally equal values.","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#ptrEq","kind":"def","line":105,"name":"ptrEq","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Util.lean#L105-L111"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">unsafe def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Util.html#withPtrAddrUnsafe\"><span class=\"name\">withPtrAddrUnsafe</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> v}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">k</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a> → <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">u₁ </span><span class=\"fn\">u₂</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#USize\">USize</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">u₁</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">k</span> <span class=\"fn\">u₂</span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">β</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Util.html#withPtrAddrUnsafe","kind":"def","line":102,"name":"withPtrAddrUnsafe","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Ut